WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:02.834
-Welcome, welcome, welcome
to "The Tonight Show,"

00:00:02.834 --> 00:00:04.400
everybody. Oh, my goodness.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:05.701
That's a crowd.

00:00:05.701 --> 00:00:10.234
♪♪

00:00:10.234 --> 00:00:11.534
Let's get to some news, guys.
We'll get --

00:00:11.534 --> 00:00:13.300
The past five days,
President Biden has

00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:15.067
been isolating with COVID,

00:00:15.067 --> 00:00:17.467
and today, his doctors said
that his symptoms are now

00:00:17.467 --> 00:00:20.067
"almost completely resolved."

00:00:20.067 --> 00:00:21.367
Yeah, that's correct.

00:00:21.367 --> 00:00:23.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:25.033
Biden's staff was like,
"Just to be safe,

00:00:25.033 --> 00:00:27.133
let's keep him isolated
till 2025."

00:00:27.133 --> 00:00:29.434
[ Laughter ]

00:00:29.434 --> 00:00:31.234
I'm happy for the president,
because usually when you hear

00:00:31.234 --> 00:00:33.200
the words "Biden" and "viral"
it's because he fell

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:36.901
up the stairs. And you go,
"How do you do that?"

00:00:36.901 --> 00:00:39.400
Yep, Biden's doctor said
that his pulse, blood pressure,

00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:42.434
and respiratory rate
remain absolutely normal.

00:00:42.434 --> 00:00:44.200
Then Biden flipped on the news
and his doctor said,

00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:46.467
"Never mind."

00:00:46.467 --> 00:00:48.868
Biden's been isolating
for the last five days.

00:00:48.868 --> 00:00:50.667
When asked how he spent
the time, Biden said,

00:00:50.667 --> 00:00:52.300
"I told one story."

00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:57.167
[ Laughter ]

00:00:57.167 --> 00:00:58.167
A good one. It was a good one.

00:00:58.167 --> 00:00:59.934
-Yeah, come on.

00:00:59.934 --> 00:01:02.567
-Biden's treatment involves
taking six pills a day

00:01:02.567 --> 00:01:04.534
for five days.

00:01:04.534 --> 00:01:06.033
All weekend long,
his pill organizer

00:01:06.033 --> 00:01:07.234
was holding on for dear life.

00:01:07.234 --> 00:01:09.467
It was like...

00:01:09.467 --> 00:01:12.534
Pfft! Monday, Tuesday,
Wednesday, Thursday, Friday.

00:01:12.534 --> 00:01:14.701
Well, as the ongoing
pilot shortage

00:01:14.701 --> 00:01:16.501
leads to more
flight cancellations,

00:01:16.501 --> 00:01:18.334
senators have introduced
a new bill

00:01:18.334 --> 00:01:22.167
to raise the mandatory
retirement age for pilots.

00:01:22.167 --> 00:01:25.567
Yeah, that's who passengers
want flying their plane,

00:01:25.567 --> 00:01:27.634
a pilot who thought
his best days are behind him.

00:01:27.634 --> 00:01:29.801
He's like, "I'm back,
I'm Maverick."

00:01:29.801 --> 00:01:31.501
And you go, "Hold on."

00:01:31.501 --> 00:01:34.934
"You're not -- Hold on,
Maverick."

00:01:34.934 --> 00:01:36.767
You'll know the pilots are old
when they start showing up

00:01:36.767 --> 00:01:41.100
to every flight 3 hours early,
like, "Alright, let's go."

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:43.000
You'll know the pilot's older
when he gets assigned

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:44.667
gate B7 and yells "Bingo."

00:01:44.667 --> 00:01:47.000
You know what I'm saying?

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:49.067
And get this, a recent
Alaska Airlines flight

00:01:49.067 --> 00:01:51.767
was delayed because two pilots
who were supposed to fly

00:01:51.767 --> 00:01:55.300
the plane had "a professional
disagreement."

00:01:55.300 --> 00:01:57.667
We actually got a hold
of the pilot's recording.

00:01:57.667 --> 00:01:58.701
Listen to this.

00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:29.033
-Oh, my God.
It was over peanuts.

00:02:29.033 --> 00:02:32.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:32.734 --> 00:02:34.100
Well, some business news
today --

00:02:34.100 --> 00:02:37.601
the barbecue grill company
Weber replaced their CEO

00:02:37.601 --> 00:02:40.667
as they continue to struggle
with a decline in sales.

00:02:40.667 --> 00:02:42.534
It's not an easy job
because the CEO is annoyed

00:02:42.534 --> 00:02:44.200
because another guy was always
standing right behind him,

00:02:44.200 --> 00:02:46.133
telling him what to do.

00:02:46.133 --> 00:02:48.367
Looks like it's time to flip
those numbers if you want to...

00:02:50.367 --> 00:02:52.100
Yeah. Apparently people
aren't excited

00:02:52.100 --> 00:02:56.434
to stand in front of a grill
when it's 150 degrees outside.

00:02:56.434 --> 00:02:58.434
Listen to this --
due to rising food prices,

00:02:58.434 --> 00:03:02.400
burgers and pizzas
are getting smaller.

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:05.501
Yep, a White Castle burger is
now the size of a postage stamp.

00:03:05.501 --> 00:03:08.634
[ Laughter ]

00:03:08.634 --> 00:03:11.267
Seriously. This is the pizza
I ordered last night.

00:03:11.267 --> 00:03:12.434
Look at that thing.

00:03:12.434 --> 00:03:14.000
-Oh, my God.

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:16.067
-I actually put the pizza
on top of that little table.

00:03:16.067 --> 00:03:18.667
It worked pretty good.

00:03:18.667 --> 00:03:20.567
Well, guys,
everyone loves TikTok.

00:03:20.567 --> 00:03:22.167
We do love it here,
but sometimes you just want

00:03:22.167 --> 00:03:23.501
to skip
the boring parts of the video

00:03:23.501 --> 00:03:24.901
and get right
to the good part.

00:03:24.901 --> 00:03:26.234
Well, it turns out you can,
alright?

00:03:26.234 --> 00:03:28.100
For instance, watching --
if you're watching this video,

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:30.434
you can skip this part.

00:03:30.434 --> 00:03:32.434
[ Laughs ]

00:03:32.434 --> 00:03:34.167
And go right to this part.

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:37.100
Ooh! Oh! There you go, yup.

00:03:37.100 --> 00:03:38.734
[ Laughs ]

00:03:38.734 --> 00:03:40.834
"Ooh! Oh!"

00:03:40.834 --> 00:03:42.100
[ Laughs ]

00:03:42.100 --> 00:03:44.200
Here's a final example.
You can skip this part.

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:47.067
-[ Humming ]

00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:49.934
And go right to this part.

00:03:54.067 --> 00:03:56.934
[ Laughter ]

00:03:56.934 --> 00:03:58.000
Yeah, yeah.

00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:04.234
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:04.234 --> 00:04:06.467
Some entertainment news, guys --
I saw Disney+

00:04:06.467 --> 00:04:09.334
just started streaming
its first R-rated movies.

00:04:09.334 --> 00:04:10.701
-Ooh.

00:04:10.701 --> 00:04:12.767
-Before this, the only
cursing you heard around Disney+

00:04:12.767 --> 00:04:14.434
is when kids
ask their parents to turn on

00:04:14.434 --> 00:04:16.567
"Encanto" again.

00:04:16.567 --> 00:04:17.767
I'm going to teach you
how to do it now.

00:04:17.767 --> 00:04:20.367
Here, just press menu
and then you go to the...

00:04:20.367 --> 00:04:22.968
Kid's chewing on
the remote control.

00:04:22.968 --> 00:04:25.033
Oh, well, this is cool.
I read that

00:04:25.033 --> 00:04:27.234
next year, NASCAR
is reportedly launching

00:04:27.234 --> 00:04:29.968
an electric racing series.

00:04:29.968 --> 00:04:31.534
It's like regular racing,
except the winner pounds

00:04:31.534 --> 00:04:34.467
a gallon of oatmilk.

00:04:34.467 --> 00:04:36.834
Did you guys see this?
Tomorrow's Mega Millions jackpot

00:04:36.834 --> 00:04:39.534
is up to $790 million.

00:04:39.534 --> 00:04:41.667
-Oh.
-$790 million.

00:04:41.667 --> 00:04:43.200
You could tell everyone
wants to win this.

00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:44.667
Even the guy who calls
the numbers every night.

00:04:44.667 --> 00:04:46.133
Listen to this.

00:04:46.133 --> 00:04:48.634
-To win that jackpot, you must
match these five white balls,

00:04:48.634 --> 00:04:51.267
plus that gold mega ball.
Here we go.

00:04:51.267 --> 00:04:53.667
First. 60. Oh, my God.

00:04:53.667 --> 00:04:56.667
Next, it's 66. Oh, my God.

00:04:56.667 --> 00:05:00.267
Then it's 14. [ Laughs ]
Kurt! I'm quitting!

00:05:00.267 --> 00:05:02.601
Then 40. [ Laughs ]

00:05:02.601 --> 00:05:04.601
I always hated
your stupid face, Kurt!

00:05:04.601 --> 00:05:06.234
And come on, 32...

00:05:06.234 --> 00:05:07.467
Mother[bleep]!

00:05:07.467 --> 00:05:09.200
-Yeah, sorry, alright.
-Kurt, I'm sorry

00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:10.767
for what I said.
-Unbelievable.

00:05:10.767 --> 00:05:13.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:14.801 --> 00:05:16.100
Well, this is going viral --

00:05:16.100 --> 00:05:18.901
a contractor is being blamed
for an unusual problem

00:05:18.901 --> 00:05:20.734
in one California town.
Take a look at this.

00:05:20.734 --> 00:05:22.534
-A city contractor in California

00:05:22.534 --> 00:05:25.067
painted the crookedest road
in the world.

00:05:25.067 --> 00:05:26.667
The strange zigzag markings

00:05:26.667 --> 00:05:28.634
are not what city officials
had in mind.

00:05:28.634 --> 00:05:32.133
A massive do-over is on the way
to replace these odd squiggles

00:05:32.133 --> 00:05:34.801
with new lane
markings done to code.

00:05:34.801 --> 00:05:37.501
Yeah. This is why you
just don't tell city employees

00:05:37.501 --> 00:05:38.767
to "just have fun with it."

00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:41.200
Well, guys, this is fun.

00:05:41.200 --> 00:05:43.734
Today is National
Aunt and Uncles Day.

00:05:43.734 --> 00:05:45.334
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yeah.

00:05:45.334 --> 00:05:46.868
I love my aunts and uncles.

00:05:46.868 --> 00:05:48.300
They've taught me so much,

00:05:48.300 --> 00:05:51.767
like the difference between
wine drunk and beer drunk.

00:05:52.801 --> 00:05:54.234
Hey, everyone's
talking about this.

00:05:54.234 --> 00:05:55.767
Tonight's Mega Millions jackpot

00:05:55.767 --> 00:05:59.868
is one of the biggest ever,
at nearly $1 billion.

00:05:59.868 --> 00:06:04.901
If you forgot to buy a ticket,
congrats, you just won $2.

00:06:05.701 --> 00:06:07.701
Yep, by tonight,
some lucky person

00:06:07.701 --> 00:06:09.167
is gonna gain
millions of dollars

00:06:09.167 --> 00:06:11.701
and hundreds of new cousins.

00:06:11.701 --> 00:06:14.234
"Hey, happy Aunt And Uncles Day.
Remember me?"

00:06:14.234 --> 00:06:16.000
That's right --
nearly a billion dollars.

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:17.434
Yeah, that kind of
money's a lot of pressure.

00:06:17.434 --> 00:06:18.901
I mean, if you win that,
next thing you know,

00:06:18.901 --> 00:06:20.801
you're buying Twitter
and having an affair with

00:06:20.801 --> 00:06:22.534
the founder of Google's wife,
you know?

00:06:22.534 --> 00:06:25.234
It's just --
It's a slippery slope.

00:06:25.234 --> 00:06:26.667
Let's get to some news
here, guys.

00:06:26.667 --> 00:06:28.434
As he continues to
recover from COVID,

00:06:28.434 --> 00:06:31.133
President Biden told reporters
he's sleeping so well

00:06:31.133 --> 00:06:34.300
that his dog had to
wake him up yesterday morning.

00:06:34.300 --> 00:06:36.300
[ Laughter ]

00:06:39.267 --> 00:06:41.767
And reporters responded with
a very nervous laugh.

00:06:41.767 --> 00:06:43.868
They're like...
[ Laughs lightly ]

00:06:43.868 --> 00:06:45.367
You know that dog was
kind of freaking out like,

00:06:45.367 --> 00:06:47.734
"Joe? Joe? Joe? Whew."

00:06:47.734 --> 00:06:50.234
You can tell Biden was tired,
'cause he tapped the dog's head

00:06:50.234 --> 00:06:53.534
and told him to come back
nine minutes later.

00:06:53.534 --> 00:06:54.634
More news from The White House.

00:06:54.634 --> 00:06:56.067
I read that
to fight climate change,

00:06:56.067 --> 00:06:57.534
the Biden administration
has pledged

00:06:57.534 --> 00:06:59.868
to plant 1 billion trees.

00:06:59.868 --> 00:07:01.834
Yep. And just
for fun, they're planting them

00:07:01.834 --> 00:07:04.334
in the middle of Trump's
golf course at Mar-a-Lago.

00:07:04.334 --> 00:07:07.434
[ Cheers and applause ]
Right in the middle.

00:07:10.868 --> 00:07:12.367
Meanwhile, this morning,
Biden woke up from

00:07:12.367 --> 00:07:16.734
his COVID fever like,
"Did I order a billion trees?"

00:07:16.734 --> 00:07:18.434
I'm sorry. Uh, yeah? Tariq?

00:07:18.434 --> 00:07:20.067
-Um, yeah, I had a question.

00:07:20.067 --> 00:07:22.634
Well, are they planting
a billion seeds

00:07:22.634 --> 00:07:23.767
or a billion trees?

00:07:23.767 --> 00:07:24.968
Because there's a difference.

00:07:24.968 --> 00:07:27.067
-You know what?
I don't really know.

00:07:27.067 --> 00:07:28.634
[ Chuckles ] Yes, Tariq.

00:07:28.634 --> 00:07:32.934
-If I had to guess,
I'd say they're planting seeds.

00:07:32.934 --> 00:07:34.567
♪♪

00:07:34.567 --> 00:07:36.868
-'Cause you gotta plant
the seeds to make the trees.

00:07:36.868 --> 00:07:38.901
-And you gotta wet the seeds
to get the leaves.

00:07:38.901 --> 00:07:40.934
-A billion trees
from a billion seeds.

00:07:40.934 --> 00:07:43.167
-We'll be seeing green
from sea-to-sea.

00:07:43.167 --> 00:07:45.367
-So much pollen,
can't help but sneeze.

00:07:45.367 --> 00:07:47.467
-But that's okay,
it's fine by me.

00:07:47.467 --> 00:07:49.501
-'Cause clean air
is what we want to see.

00:07:49.501 --> 00:07:51.801
-To the birds and
the insects and the bumblebees.

00:07:51.801 --> 00:07:53.934
-We'll be oh-so-happy
to enjoy that breeze.

00:07:53.934 --> 00:07:56.067
-A billion trees
from a billion seeds?

00:07:56.067 --> 00:07:58.434
I got one answer,
yes, please.

00:07:58.434 --> 00:08:02.234
-♪ Seeds and trees ♪

00:08:02.234 --> 00:08:04.267
♪ Planting the crops ♪

00:08:04.267 --> 00:08:06.234
♪ Ready or not ♪

00:08:06.234 --> 00:08:09.167
-"Seeds and Trees Mixtape,
2022."

00:08:09.167 --> 00:08:11.000
[ Air horn blows ]

00:08:11.000 --> 00:08:13.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:16.300 --> 00:08:18.701
-What is going on?
-Man.

00:08:18.701 --> 00:08:20.501
I saw that -- Guys, today,

00:08:20.501 --> 00:08:23.100
former President Trump returned
to Washington, D.C.,

00:08:23.100 --> 00:08:25.567
for the first time
since leaving office.

00:08:25.567 --> 00:08:27.534
Trump said, "Well,
since I'm still the president,

00:08:27.534 --> 00:08:29.801
it only makes sense I stop by."

00:08:32.334 --> 00:08:35.634
Switching gears, T-Mobile
has agreed to pay its customers

00:08:35.634 --> 00:08:38.167
$350 million in a settlement

00:08:38.167 --> 00:08:40.534
over a massive data breach.

00:08:40.534 --> 00:08:42.300
We actually have
their lawyer on the line

00:08:42.300 --> 00:08:43.434
to explain their settlement.

00:08:43.434 --> 00:08:44.667
Yeah, sir, are you there?

00:08:44.667 --> 00:08:47.200
-Hi, Jimmy.
Thank you for having me.

00:08:47.200 --> 00:08:50.200
"Tonight Show"...to be here.

00:08:52.067 --> 00:08:54.801
-Sorry? This is
a massive settlement here,

00:08:54.801 --> 00:08:56.667
so how are you feeling?

00:08:56.667 --> 00:09:00.133
-Well, now that...settlement...
completed...

00:09:00.133 --> 00:09:02.901
try to relax...
raspberry custard...

00:09:02.901 --> 00:09:06.367
nipples...pet hamster.

00:09:06.367 --> 00:09:08.100
-I'm sorry. You're cutting out.

00:09:08.100 --> 00:09:10.501
Can you say that again?
-Of course.

00:09:10.501 --> 00:09:12.901
I was just saying now that
the settlement is completed,

00:09:12.901 --> 00:09:15.667
I...go home...
raspberry custard...

00:09:15.667 --> 00:09:18.334
nipples...pet hamster.

00:09:19.567 --> 00:09:21.701
-Sorry. It's still a bit choppy.

00:09:21.701 --> 00:09:23.734
It's not really making sense.

00:09:23.734 --> 00:09:25.467
Can you switch to Wi-Fi?

00:09:25.467 --> 00:09:28.400
-Uh, sure, Jimmy. How's this?
Can you hear me now?

00:09:28.400 --> 00:09:30.501
-It's much better. Thank you.
-Great.

00:09:30.501 --> 00:09:32.667
I was just saying, now that the
settlement is completed,

00:09:32.667 --> 00:09:34.000
I want to relax.

00:09:34.000 --> 00:09:36.367
I think I might go home
and smear raspberry custard

00:09:36.367 --> 00:09:38.133
on my nipples and let my
pet hamster nibble on it

00:09:38.133 --> 00:09:39.567
until it tickles.

00:09:39.567 --> 00:09:41.801
That usually helps me calm down.
-Alright, good luck with that.

00:09:41.801 --> 00:09:44.567
Thank you for joining us today.
The lawyer from...

00:09:44.567 --> 00:09:46.434
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:46.434 --> 00:09:48.033
I don't know.

00:09:51.133 --> 00:09:52.467
Hey, have you guys seen this?

00:09:52.467 --> 00:09:54.467
There's an online movement of
people who want Instagram

00:09:54.467 --> 00:09:56.901
to go back to being
a photo-sharing app

00:09:56.901 --> 00:09:59.868
and are criticizing it
for trying to copy TikTok.

00:09:59.868 --> 00:10:02.200
You know things
are bad when Instagram

00:10:02.200 --> 00:10:04.200
is getting bullied on Instagram.

00:10:04.200 --> 00:10:05.367
Hey, guys, get this.

00:10:05.367 --> 00:10:10.767
A dating site for
anti-vaxxers called Unjected

00:10:10.767 --> 00:10:15.234
had -- this is real -- had all
of its user data exposed online.

00:10:15.234 --> 00:10:16.601
Yeah. But don't worry.

00:10:16.601 --> 00:10:19.534
Everyone is doing their own
research on how to fix it.

00:10:21.434 --> 00:10:24.400
Users' names, birthdays, e-mail
addresses, and home addresses

00:10:24.400 --> 00:10:26.367
were exposed,
but on the plus side,

00:10:26.367 --> 00:10:29.868
their data is one step closer
to herd immunity.

00:10:29.868 --> 00:10:31.100
Hey, listen to this.

00:10:31.100 --> 00:10:33.901
According to a new report,
the Chevy Silverado

00:10:33.901 --> 00:10:35.834
is the most stolen vehicle
in the country.

00:10:35.834 --> 00:10:37.133
-Ooh!

00:10:37.133 --> 00:10:39.501
-And Chevy decided to use
this fact as a selling point

00:10:39.501 --> 00:10:40.634
in their latest commercial.

00:10:40.634 --> 00:10:42.000
Watch this.

00:10:42.000 --> 00:10:45.834
-So, our Silverado is the
most stolen vehicle in America.

00:10:45.834 --> 00:10:49.400
Well, maybe it's because of
our Duramax turbo-diesel engine.

00:10:49.400 --> 00:10:52.267
Or maybe it's because of
our automatic emergency braking.

00:10:52.267 --> 00:10:55.133
Or just maybe it's because
our doors don't lock,

00:10:55.133 --> 00:10:56.968
there's no alarm system,
and you can start the truck

00:10:56.968 --> 00:10:58.200
just by breathing
on the steering wheel.

00:10:58.200 --> 00:10:59.501
-[ Breathes deeply ]

00:10:59.501 --> 00:11:02.801
-Chevy Silverado --
apparently, they're free now.

00:11:02.801 --> 00:11:05.868
-I saw that today.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:11:10.501 --> 00:11:13.000
Hey, I saw a house listing
that's getting a lot of

00:11:13.000 --> 00:11:14.834
attention for
its strange design.

00:11:14.834 --> 00:11:16.167
Check this thing out.

00:11:16.167 --> 00:11:18.334
-An unusual property
in Pismo Beach, California,

00:11:18.334 --> 00:11:20.334
is attracting
a lot of attention.

00:11:20.334 --> 00:11:23.467
